-- title:
--   Regularity of a stalk pro-representing a regular local ring
-- statement:
--   Let $q$ be a prime. Let $Y$ be a scheme (in the bottom universe) equipped with a morphism $\pi_Y : Y \to \operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_q$ which is locally of finite type, and let $y \in Y$ be a point whose singleton is closed and which satisfies $\pi_Y(y) =$ the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}_q$; write $S = \mathcal{O}_{Y,y}$ for the stalk of the structure presheaf at $y$. Let $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$ be a commutative ring which is a domain, a discrete valuation ring, of characteristic zero, and a $\mathbb{Z}_q$-algebra such that the ideal generated by the image of $q$ is maximal; write $k$ for its residue field and $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}} \to k$ for its residue map. Let $\bar x : S \to k$ be a ring homomorphism whose kernel is the maximal ideal of $S$. Let $R$ be a commutative regular local ring which is an $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra and is adically complete for its maximal ideal, let $\mathrm{res}_R : R \to k$ be a ring homomorphism with $\mathrm{res}_R \circ (\text{structure map } \mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}} \to R)$ equal to the residue map of $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$, and let $\varphi : S \to R$ satisfy $\mathrm{res}_R \circ \varphi = \bar x$. Assume the following universal property: for every Artinian local $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra $A$ and every surjective ring homomorphism $\mathrm{res}_A : A \to k$ whose composition with the structure map $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}} \to A$ is the residue map of $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$, and every ring homomorphism $\psi : S \to A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A \circ \psi = \bar x$, there is a unique $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra homomorphism $\chi : R \to A$ with $\mathrm{res}_A \circ \chi = \mathrm{res}_R$ and $\chi \circ \varphi = \psi$. Assume finally that the image of $q$ in $R$ is nonzero. Then $S$ is a regular local ring and the image of $q$ in $S$ is nonzero.
--
--   This is the descent of regularity from a pro-representing hull to the local ring itself: if the functor of $k$-pointed Artinian-local-algebra points of $Y$ at $y$ is pro-represented by a complete regular local $\mathcal{O}^{\mathrm{nr}}$-algebra in which $q$ remains nonzero, then $\mathcal{O}_{Y,y}$ is itself regular with $q \neq 0$, without assuming flatness or passing to the completion of $\mathcal{O}_{Y,y}$. It is used in the study of the moduli schemes of fake elliptic curves arising in the Čerednik–Drinfeld theory, where it yields regularity and flatness statements at closed points of the special fibre; the finiteness of the residue field of the stalk comes from [`AlgebraicGeometry.finite_residueField_stalk_of_isClosed_of_locallyOfFiniteType`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.finite_residueField_stalk_of_isClosed_of_locallyOfFiniteType), and the construction of Artinian test points from [`IsLocalRing.exists_ringHom_comp_eq_of_natCast_notMem_maximalIdeal_sq`](thm.html#IsLocalRing.exists_ringHom_comp_eq_of_natCast_notMem_maximalIdeal_sq).
